==== 3. Is the oscillation inside the feedback loop? (current vs x at the peak frequency) ====
  39 g hole-up   : measured i/x 154 A/m at -6 deg | controller 151 A/m at -2.4 deg
  42 g hole-up   : measured i/x 183 A/m at -14 deg | controller 151 A/m at -2.6 deg
  39 g hole-down : measured i/x 154 A/m at -8 deg | controller 152 A/m at -4.7 deg
PASS: the 2.4 Hz current is the controller's response to the measured x (gain and phase as the controller prescribes)
  -> the oscillation is SUSTAINED through the loop: the only power source is the coil, and the coil's
     2.4 Hz current is produced by the controller from the measured x (a free mechanical mode would
     decay, as the 42 g ringing does).

